{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>From the El of your father.</b> And this too you had from the blessed El in that He is the El of your father, who told me that the elevation would come to my seed after the lowliness, as it says: וְהָיָה זַרְעֲךָ כַּעֲפַר הָאָרֶץ וּפָרַצְתָּ (Genesis 28:14)." "<b>And He will help you.</b> So that you fall no more." "<b>And from Shaddai.</b> And from El Shaddai, who said to me: אֲנִי אֵל שַׁדַּי פְּרֵה וּרְבֵה גּוֹי וּקְהַל גּוֹיִם יִהְיֶה מִמְּךָ (Genesis 35:11) — from Him came this elevation to you." "<b>And may He bless you.</b> Without intermediary — not like His blessing to Manasseh and Ephraim, which was through the redeeming angel (Genesis 48:16), and not like Isaac's blessing to Esau and Moses' blessing to those who enter the land, which was from the mouth of a man; but He Himself will be the one who blesses, as Isaac said to Jacob: וְאֵל שַׁדַּי יְבָרֵךְ אוֹתְךָ. And so Moses to Israel before their sin with the spies, as it says: וִיבָרֵךְ אֶתְכֶם כַּאֲשֶׁר דִּבֶּר לָכֶם (Deuteronomy 1:11)." "<b>Blessings of heaven above.</b> In such manner that the number of your days be fulfilled (Exodus 23:27)." "<b>Blessings of the deep that couches beneath.</b> And they are blessings in foodstuffs and in wealth." "<b>Blessings of breasts and womb.</b> And they are blessings in children — the reverse of רֶחֶם מַשְׁכִּיל וְשָׁדַיִם צוֹמְקִים (Hosea 9:14)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:32.717962652Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}